  "termination": "completed",
  "answer": "All three modules are updated. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## `defaults.mjs`\n- `DEFAULT_OPTIONS` now exposes all three defaults: `{ precision: 2, prefix: '', unitLabel: '' }`.\n- Wrapped in `Object.freeze(...)` so it can never be mutated (the old `Object.assign(DEFAULT_OPTIONS, ...)` mutation bug is gone).\n\n## `resolver.mjs`\n- `resolveOptions(overrides)` returns a **fresh** object each call, seeded from the frozen defaults and overridden by supplied own fields — no shared mutable state.\n- `undefined` (or no argument) means no overrides.\n- Rejects `null`, non-objects, and arrays with `TypeError`.\n- Rejects unknown keys with `TypeError`.\n- `precision` must be an integer 0–4, else `RangeError`.\n- `prefix` and `unitLabel` must be strings, else `TypeError`.\n- Only own fields are read (via `hasOwnProperty`), so inherited properties are ignored.\n\n## `formatter.mjs`\n- `formatValue(value, overrides)` accepts only finite numbers, else `TypeError`.\n- Delegates option resolution to `resolveOptions`.\n- Appends `\" \" + unitLabel` only when `unitLabel` is nonempty.\n- Old call forms still work (`overrides` defaults to `undefined`).\n\n## Behavior verification\n- `formatValue(12.345)` → `\"12.35\"` ✓\n- `formatValue(12.34, { precision: 1, prefix: '~' })` → `\"~12.3\"` ✓\n- `formatValue(12.3, { unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `\"12.30 kg\"` ✓\n- `formatValue(12.3, { precision: 1, prefix: '~', unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `\"~12.3 kg\"` ✓\n- `resolveOptions({ unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `{ precision: 2, prefix: '', unitLabel: 'kg' }` ✓\n\nThe existing `public.test.mjs` assertions are all satisfied, and the new validation/immutability requirements are covered.",
